\section{Pinned Memory and Asynchronous Transfer}

\subsection{Pinned Host Buffers}

Telemetry values are expanded into pinned host arrays:

\begin{quote}
``std::fill(h\_plus.begin(), h\_plus.end(), ligo.h\_plus * |gaia.vx|);''
\end{quote}

Pinned memory enables high-throughput DMA transfers to the GPU.

\subsection{Non-Blocking CUDA Streams}

The ingestion pipeline uses two independent streams:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Transfer Stream:} Handles asynchronous host-to-device copies.
    \item \textbf{Compute Stream:} Executes tensor projections and Lindblad passes.
\end{itemize}

Both streams are created with:

\begin{quote}
``cudaStreamCreateWithFlags(... cudaStreamNonBlocking)''
\end{quote}

This eliminates default-stream serialization and allows continuous overlap 
of data movement and computation.

